# Dreaming in Spw — 2026-11-11
#
# A reading of the story consumer (the serial, its lanes, its desk and its ?/ door) for where characters could dream in Spw, what would make that engaging to play, and how a dream could route a reader through an intricate story.
# The consumer was read, never written. Everything below is an offer for its maker; the counts are from its released chapters and canon, read through this repo's parser.

#>journal_2026_11_11_dreaming_in_spw
#:cache #!observation
#:layer #!pragmatics

^["entry"]{
 date: "2026-11-11"
 kind: #observation
 base: "the story consumer's main at c133fa5, read only; this repo at 9ef3d223"
 method: "read the consumer's canon index, almanac bracework, characters, elaboration, shelves, gossip and kitchens, liminal physics, AST play, gradients, three lands, realm powers, tellings, Book Two and the reading grammar, and the heads of rooms, story-boonhonk, pie rules, the route reader, the table renderer and the living slots; walked chapters 1 to 15 for every table's bracework move, every room signature with its air, and every living slot; grouped the moves by this repo's likeness shape; read one dream address through the consumer's own route reader"
 limits: "nothing was built or played; several surfaces were read in part (rooms to line 60 of 112, story-boonhonk by its headings and four blocks); Book Two has two released chapters, so every Book One against Book Two count is small; the price reading rests on four moves; no view was checked for what it does with a route's @ and ~ beyond a search; no room in the 81 carries a drafting status"
}

^["review"]{
 tilde_glosses: "the consumer gives ~ five glosses: the bracework bench says one thing dreaming of being another; a room signature says something not yet happened (room-signature.mjs); the reading grammar says a scene seed held without asserting it happened; the lanes say what lasts a while; a ?/ route says a motif, what keeps coming back. Only the bench says dream; the reading that all five are registers of dreaming is offered under grammar"
 rooms: "81 rooms over 15 chapters, each signed op + container(place) + @keeper; ~ is Book One's commonest room sigil, 12 of 67 rooms, 9 of them < > passages and 8 kept by the dog; Book Two has 0 of 14, and @ rises from 1 of 67 to 2 of 14"
 furrow: "warm_furrow is the one place signed twice: ~{warm_furrow}@boof in chapter 1 and @{warm_furrow}@boof in chapter 14; the consumer's rooms surface already gives this pair as its own example, the same furrow now seen"
 endings: "six of thirteen Book One chapters end in a ~ passage kept by the dog or a stranger (4, 6, 7, 8, 10, 12); both Book Two chapters end in a = lean"
 table: "each chapter's table (At the table, chapter-render.mjs renderTable: a game-master's page with place, light, people, hooks, a die of encounters, finds, a bracework move with Does and Costs, the page's own dice, and a question for the table) already makes the chapter a place to play"
 moves: "the fifteen bracework moves fall into nine shapes; [_ @ _] five times (1, 5, 13, 14, 15) and <_ ~ _> three times (2, 3, 6), with {bud ~ honey} the one ~ move kept in a room (11); both Book Two moves are watching windows"
 night: "four of fifteen move costs end at sleep or a night: until you sleep (2), dark for a night (6), until the next still night (8), for a night (14)"
 living_slots: "69 living slots carry 343 faces the maker wrote, each turning on a clock (40 by the hour, 14 by the day, 15 by the minute; living.mjs variantFor, whose salt already varies the face); the first face is the book's own words, and the table rolls them as the page's own dice. Chapter 2's rehearsed-futures slot turns by the minute through doors opening onto a morning she almost knew"
 carriers: "every character card carries ~escape and ~eased; five of eleven escapes (genie, porter, clerk, figure, clown) say what a reader is for a carry as them, so those carries are already a reader dreaming of being someone; the other six say what it is like near them"
 kitchen: "wish-kitchen.mjs gives each character an operator over a wish's tastes: the dog a dot product (only what points where she already is), BoneWAP only what is declared, BoonWAP a scaled sum, BaneWAP a cross product (perpendicular, true the bad way), the clown bigger with a crust, the mime as a busy kitchen reads it, the figure nobody has said"
}

^["grammar"]{
 # A dream needs no new sigil role: it is ~ in the container it is kept in, seen through a keeper.
 reading: "a dream is what each gloss of ~ describes at once: something not yet happened, held without being asserted, lasting a while, coming back, one thing being another. Read so, dreaming is the land's word for the role ~ already plays, not a new one"
 containers: "the room kinds are already the ways to be in a dream: [moth ~ morning] watched only, {moth ~ morning} stood in for a minute, (moth ~ morning) shared and kept only if every dreamer arrives, <moth ~ morning> gone through and never stayed in; the four parse whole as four shapes over one set of words"
 direction: "the four ~ moves face two ways: moth to morning and bud to honey dream ahead, salt to sea and dent to street dream back. Most of the ahead costs are time (a beat late until you sleep; the almanac a day short; the next wait a minute longer) and most of the back costs are place (everything salt-stiff; the whale rises to look; the round one post short; somebody walks the wrong way home). Three clauses do not fit: chapter 11's box runs on borrowed warmth the ants will notice, chapter 3's whale believes for an hour, and chapter 6's lantern is dark for a night. Four moves are a reading, not a law; it agrees with the consumer's guard that no mechanic gives foresight for free"
 keeper: "@keeper says whose dream it is; held keepers keep none"
}

^["imagined"]{
 # An offer, composed only from released airs: the dog's eight ~ rooms in chapter order, as one night. It parses whole.
 boof: "~{night}@boof[ ~{warm_furrow} ~<hill_stairs> ~<iron_gate> ~<rocky_ridge> ~<rear_archway> ~{quince_rise} [] ~<moon_lane> ~{last_line} ], each room carrying its own air"
 refrain: "warm is the dream's refrain: the ground keeping something warm (1), a slice kept warm in waxed paper (6), the well's answer warm against her ribs (8), the slice still warm in its paper; she does not know why she carries it (10). It ends in a room with one wall unbuilt that anybody might walk into (13), and Book Two's furrow is watched"
 blank: "quince_rise's air names a held thing, so in the dream it is an empty frame, the clerk's box for what you do not know"
 others: "the echo keeps a forked path that meets itself again (2), the Fool a mouthpiece of amber steam, not sound, not yet (9), the Genie an upstream grove where he becomes an echo you can visit (12); the stranger's long alley (7) is left unglossed, since that thread is unassigned on purpose"
}

^["play"]{
 # Each names the seam it would extend. All would sit behind a trial switch.
 night_settles: "the reader's local midnight (route-events localDay) is when night-priced costs clear, and the clearing is shown as the cast's dream, waiting on the next visit; gradients.spw already says ~ is worth most on a return"
 night_clock: "a fourth clock for the living slots, the night, salted by the dreamer: the chapters the reader read today, each slot turned to the face this dreamer would turn it to. Every face is one the maker already wrote, so nobody says anything new; the slots that turned are what changed, which is how a reader learns a character by difference"
 day_refilled: "past the slots, a dream could refill the day's shape (rooms read, the carry run) from the dreamer's registry words; choosing them by the dreamer's wish-kitchen operator is an analogy until words have a space to point in, and the shelves' five-part signature is the one that exists"
 price_by_direction: "a reader who turns a dream ahead pays in tempo (the lag the lanes already lend), one who turns it back pays in place (a lane one post short); ahead never reaches past a released chapter"
 nightmare_switch: "a dream that leans bane comes true the bad way and, being BaneWAP's, keeps an off switch somewhere in it; finding it is the play, and the fear has a floor"
 seed_only: "a dream can carry a trope from seed to hint (elaboration's ~ and ? stages) and never further: a dream does not assert, so it cannot name, turn or pay"
 shared: "( ) dreams for the together span: two readers or two keepers must both arrive, and if either wakes both do"
 collect: "a reader's map marks a place ~ while it has only been dreamed and @ once it has been met awake, as the furrow is in the canon; a dream card is collected by its shape"
}

^["routing"]{
 address: "the consumer's daily route with @boof and ~warm_furrow appended reads today through its route reader as the day event, perspective boof, motif warm_furrow, and writeRoute writes the same parts back in its fixed order. The reader glosses @ as the maker a surface is seen from, so @ as a dreamer is a reading; the seam is SURFACE_READS, where a surface says what its own parts mean, plus a day view that reads them. The texture page reads ~ only for its finds, and no day view was found reading @ or ~"
 sideways: "a ~ passage could open onto rooms the reader has already read that share its shape (the three <_ ~ _> moves, the five [_ @ _] windows), which is the realm-powers guard exactly: a second way out goes sideways, never ahead"
 table: "at the table, a dream is a roll: the page's own dice already list every slot's faces, so a night roll is a table move a game-master can make without the page"
 sealed: "AST play asks whether a sealed region could be opened by a ~ door from another surface; a dream is that door told in the land's words"
 ring: "chapter 14 writes chapter 1's shape ([week @ morning], [map @ field]) and chapter 15 does not write chapter 2's ([gate @ storm], <moth ~ morning>); one of two seats rhymes, so a dream that routes seat to seat across rings of thirteen is the maker's to want, not a pattern found"
}

!["guards"]{
 # The consumer's own, applied to dreams.
 words: "nobody says anything new; a dream recomposes released words"
 roles: "a sigil keeps its role; a dream that needs ~ to mean something new is the wrong dream"
 held: "the figure, the hat and the Egg stay held; a dream touching a held word dreams a blank box, and the figure's dream is nobody has said"
 foresight: "no foresight for free, and never past a released chapter"
 sorting: "no reader is sorted by what they dream, and no shelf is a moral ranking"
 switch: "new behaviour waits behind a trial switch"
}

?["open"]{
 book_two: "Is Book Two's missing ~ a choice, a book that watches where Book One dreamed, or two chapters of chance? At Book One's rate, 14 rooms would hold two or three"
 figure: "Does the figure dream, or is that the one card the land leaves blank?"
 mimes: "Do mimes dream in the words they carry, and would showing them break the rule that mimes never speak?"
 where: "Where does a dream wait: the end card, the day route, the almanac, or with the crows the ants give scraps to?"
}

^["workbench"]{
 candidate_ask: "refill a rhyme's template with new words and hold the result to the same shape, and index read subtrees by shape key so a host can open sideways doors; a candidate for the consumer to ask for, not built"
}
